This crate (`symphonia-codec-ilbc`) is a pure-Rust iLBC (Internet Low Bitrate Codec, RFC 3951)
decoder. The Rust code is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of
Project Symphonia.

The bitstream unpacking, the LSF/LPC, state, codebook and gain reconstruction, the frame loss
concealment and the output high-pass filter follow FFmpeg's `libavcodec/ilbcdec.c`, and the tables
(`src/tables.rs`) are copied from `libavcodec/ilbcdata.h`. FFmpeg is distributed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. Those files are themselves derived from the
WebRTC iLBC fixed-point reference implementation (RFC 3951), under the BSD-3-Clause license
below. The LGPL-2.1+ terms apply to the derived portions.

The test fixtures (`tests/fixtures`) were produced with the libilbc encoder (a packaging of the
WebRTC iLBC codec, BSD-3-Clause) from its `sample.pcm`. libilbc is not a dependency.

